#: src/development.md
msgid ""
"GitHub Actions でも同じ順に流す（`.github/workflows/ci.yml`）。試験は、試験ご"
"とに一時の DB を作る。workflow の `image` は、`Containerfile` を arm64 の "
"runner で build し、[image に入る物](release.md#image-に入る物) を確かめ"
"（`ci/check-image.sh`）、空の image の中で起きて置いて読めること・止める合図"
"で終わること・起こし直しても残ることを見る（`ci/smoke-image.sh`）。release "
"の workflow も、同じ 2 つを push の前に流す。workflow の `cli` は、release に"
"付ける CLI を macOS（arm64）の runner で、出す時と同じ script（`ci/build-"
"cli.sh`）で作り、binary の形・つながる library・版・秘密の走査を確かめ（`ci/"
"check-cli.sh`）、その binary を同じ commit のサーバーに向けて打つ。"
msgstr ""
"GitHub Actions runs the same steps in the same order (`.github/workflows/"
"ci.yml`). Each test creates its own temporary DB. The workflow's `image` "
"builds the `Containerfile` on an arm64 runner, verifies [What goes into the "
"image](release.md#what-goes-into-the-image) (`ci/check-image.sh`), and "
"checks that, inside the empty image, it starts and can store and read, that "
"it exits on the stop signal, and that data remains after a restart (`ci/"
"smoke-image.sh`). The release workflow also runs the same two before the "
"push. The workflow's `cli` builds the CLI attached to a release on a macOS "
"(arm64) runner with the same script used for publishing (`ci/build-cli.sh`), "
"verifies the binary's format, linked libraries, version, and the secret scan "
"(`ci/check-cli.sh`), and runs that binary against the server from the same "
"commit."

#: src/development.md
msgid ""
"API の形（URL・引数の名・JSON の欄）を変える時は、先に [API の仕様]"
"(api.md#api-の版を上げる時上げない時) の「API の版を上げる時・上げない時」を"
"見る。変えたら、roster の `tpm page`（`cli/src/commands/page.ts`）と、その偽"
"の置き場（`cli/test/helpers.ts` の `FakeStore`）も合わせて直す。roster の CI "
"が、この repo の決めた版に向けて、つなぎの試験を流す。"
msgstr ""
"Before changing the shape of an endpoint (URLs, parameter names, JSON "
"fields), first read \"When to bump the API version, and when not to\" in "
"[API specification](api.md#when-to-bump-the-api-version-and-when-not-to). "
"After changing it, also update `tpm page` in roster (`cli/src/commands/"
"page.ts`) and its fake page store (`FakeStore` in `cli/test/helpers.ts`) to "
"match. The CI in roster runs the integration tests against the version this "
"repo specifies."

#: src/development.md
msgid ""
"**SQL を変えた時**: SQL は `query!` が build の時に `.sqlx/` と突き合わせる。"
"SQL か `migrations/` を変えたら、一時の DB を作って作り直し、commit する（忘"
"れると CI の `cargo sqlx prepare --check` が落ちる）。`sqlx-cli` の版は "
"workflow の `SQLX_CLI_VERSION` と合わせる。"
msgstr ""
"**When you change SQL**: `query!` checks SQL against `.sqlx/` at build time. "
"If you change SQL or `migrations/`, create a temporary DB, regenerate `.sqlx/"
"`, and commit it (if you forget, `cargo sqlx prepare --check` in CI fails). "
"Keep the `sqlx-cli` version in sync with `SQLX_CLI_VERSION` in the workflow."

#: src/development.md
msgid "sqlite://$PWD/target/dev.db"
msgstr "sqlite://$PWD/target/dev.db"

#: src/development.md
msgid ""
"**当てた移行の SQL は変えない**: 動いている DB が、当てた SQL の中身を覚えて"
"いる。表を変える時は `migrations/` に次の番号の file を足し、`tests/"
"migrations.rs` の一覧に 1 行足す（前からある行が変わると、試験が落ちる）。"
msgstr ""
"**Never change an applied migration**: A running DB remembers the contents "
"of the SQL that was applied. To change a table, add a file with the next "
"number to `migrations/` and add one line to the list in `tests/"
"migrations.rs` (if an existing line changes, the test fails)."

#: src/development.md
msgid ""
"**表を変えたら、章も直す**: 表・列・型・空を許すか・主キーと一意と索引を変え"
"たら、同じ PR で [DB の作り](db.md) と、表を足したなら [用語集](glossary.md) "
"も直す。`tests/schema_doc.rs` が、移行を当てた DB と章を突き合わせ、食い違え"
"ば落ちる。"
msgstr ""
"**When you change a table, update the chapter too**: When you change tables, "
"columns, types, nullability, primary keys, unique constraints, or indexes, "
"update [DB schema](db.md) in the same PR, and the [Glossary](glossary.md) "
"too if you add a table. `tests/schema_doc.rs` compares the migrated DB with "
"the chapter and fails if they differ."

#: src/development.md
msgid ""
"**版を上げる**: `Cargo.toml` の `[workspace.package]` の `version` を上げ"
"（サーバーと `crates/` の crate が同じ版になる。`Cargo.lock` も変わる）、"
"`CHANGELOG.md` に、API の版が変わったかを書く。"
msgstr ""
"**Bump the version**: Bump `version` under `[workspace.package]` in "
"`Cargo.toml` (the server and the crates in `crates/` get the same version; "
"`Cargo.lock` changes too), and note in `CHANGELOG.md` whether the API "
"version changed."

#: src/development.md
msgid ""
"**crate を上げる**: `.cargo/config.toml` の `global-min-publish-age` が、公開"
"から 2 日たっていない版を選ばせない（Cargo 1.100 から）。上げる時は `cargo "
"update` → 試験 → PR。`cargo install` はこの決まりを見ないので、道具は版を書い"
"て入れる。"
msgstr ""
"**Update crates**: `global-min-publish-age` in `.cargo/config.toml` prevents "
"selecting versions published less than 2 days ago (since Cargo 1.100). To "
"update: `cargo update` → tests → PR. `cargo install` does not honor this "
"rule, so install tools with an explicit version."

#: src/development.md
msgid ""
"**弱点と license の見張り**: workflow の `advisories` が `cargo deny check "
"advisories licenses`（設定は `deny.toml`）を、PR ごとと週に 1 度流す。"
"`deny.toml` に無い license の crate が入ると落ちる。"
msgstr ""
"**Vulnerability and license monitoring**: The workflow's `advisories` runs "
"`cargo deny check advisories licenses` (configured in `deny.toml`) on every "
"PR and once a week. It fails when a crate with a license not listed in "
"`deny.toml` comes in."

#: src/development.md
msgid ""
"**workflow の action**: commit の SHA で固定する（tag は後から中身が替わりう"
"る）。"
msgstr ""
"**Workflow actions**: Pin them by commit SHA (the contents behind a tag can "
"be replaced later)."

#: src/development.md
msgid ""
"**main を守る決まり**: GitHub の ruleset「main: CI が通らないと merge できな"
"い」（Settings → Rules → Rulesets）が、`main` への変更に、CI の `test`・"
"`image`・`advisories`・`docs`・`cli` の 5 つが通っていることを求める。PR は、"
"5 つが通るまで merge できない。repo の admin は、この決まりを bypass できるの"
"で、`main` への直の push は通る（GitHub の必須の check には「PR だけに効かせ"
"る」選び方が無いので、直の push を通すには bypass になる）。admin は、わざと"
"選べば（画面の bypass の印・`gh pr merge --admin`）PR も CI を通さずに merge "
"できてしまうので、使わない。workflow の job の名を変えたら、ruleset の check "
"の名も合わせて直す（合わないと、PR がいつまでも merge できない）。"
msgstr ""
"**Branch protection for main**: The GitHub ruleset \"main: cannot merge "
"unless CI passes\" (Settings → Rules → Rulesets) requires that the five CI "
"checks `test`, `image`, `advisories`, `docs`, and `cli` pass for changes to "
"`main`. A PR cannot be merged until all five pass. Repo admins can bypass "
"this rule, so direct pushes to `main` go through (GitHub's required checks "
"have no option to \"apply to PRs only\", so allowing direct pushes means a "
"bypass). An admin who deliberately chooses to (the bypass checkbox in the "
"UI, or `gh pr merge --admin`) can also merge a PR without CI passing, so do "
"not use it. If you rename a workflow job, also update the check name in the "
"ruleset to match (otherwise PRs can never be merged)."

#: src/development.md
msgid "一覧の UI の試験"
msgstr "List UI tests"

#: src/development.md
msgid ""
"一覧の UI は、HTML の字を `tests/ui.rs` が見て、browser でしか見えない物"
"（script の動き・色・幅での並び）を `e2e/` の試験が見る。`e2e/` は "
"[Playwright](https://playwright.dev/) の試験（TypeScript）で、同じ commit の "
"`pagetray-server` を一時の DB で起こし、本物の browser（Chromium）で開く。"
"Node が要るのはこの folder の中だけで、image にも CLI にも入らない。"
msgstr ""
"For the list UI, `tests/ui.rs` checks the text of the HTML, and the tests in "
"`e2e/` check what can only be seen in a browser (what the script does, "
"colors, and the layout at each width). `e2e/` holds [Playwright](https://"
"playwright.dev/) tests (TypeScript): they start the `pagetray-server` of the "
"same commit with a temporary DB and open it in a real browser (Chromium). "
"Node is needed only inside this folder, and it goes into neither the image "
"nor the CLI."

#: src/development.md
msgid "# 初めの 1 度だけ。試験用の Chromium を入れる\n"
msgstr "# Only the first time. Installs the Chromium used by the tests\n"

#: src/development.md
msgid "chrome"
msgstr "chrome"

#: src/development.md
msgid "# この機械の Chrome を使う（Chromium を入れなくてよい）\n"
msgstr ""
"# Use the Chrome installed on this machine (no need to install Chromium)\n"

#: src/development.md
msgid ""
"**CI**: workflow の `ui` が PR ごとに流す。落ちると、画面の絵と操作の記録が "
"artifact（`ui-report`）に残る。`ui` は、main を守る決まりの必須の check に、"
"まだ入れていない（時々落ちないことを見てから足す）。"
msgstr ""
"**CI**: The workflow's `ui` job runs them on every PR. When a test fails, a "
"screenshot and a trace of the steps are kept in the artifact (`ui-report`). "
"`ui` is not yet one of the required checks of the rule protecting main (it "
"will be added once it has been seen not to fail intermittently)."

#: src/development.md
msgid ""
"**読むだけの試験**: 題に `@smoke` が付いた試験（`e2e/tests/smoke.spec.ts`）"
"は、何も置かず、何が置かれていても通る物だけを見る。`PAGETRAY_E2E_URL=http://"
"127.0.0.1:8801 pnpm test` と打つと、サーバーを起こさず、動いている置き場に向"
"けて、この試験だけが流れる（置く試験は、設定が流させない）。版を上げた後の確"
"かめに使う（[動かす](run.md#確かめる) の「確かめる」）。"
msgstr ""
"**Read-only test**: The test with `@smoke` in its title (`e2e/tests/"
"smoke.spec.ts`) puts nothing and checks only things that hold whatever is in "
"the store. With `PAGETRAY_E2E_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8801 pnpm test`, no "
"server is started and only this test runs, against the running store (the "
"configuration does not let the tests that put pages run). It is used to "
"verify after raising the version (\"Verify\" in [Running](run.md#verify))."

#: src/development.md
msgid ""
"**試験を足す**: `e2e/tests/` に `*.spec.ts` を足す。ページは `helpers.ts` の "
"`place` で置き、区画（操作の帯・絞り込みの列・一覧の列・本文の枠と、Key の画"
"面の file の枠・上げる枠）は `helpers.ts` の関数で選ぶ。file は `placeFile` "
"で置き、上げる枠の試験は `input[type=file]` に `setInputFiles` で file を渡"
"す。試験は同じ置き場に 1 本ずつ順に流れるので、試験ごとに別の project の名を"
"使う。新着を見る試験（一覧の列の差し替えと新着の印）は、`openLive` で開いてか"
"ら置く（知らせにつながる前に置いたページの知らせは届かない）。新着の印は一覧"
"の列を下へ送っている時に出るので、`scrollList` で送ってから置く。大きな file "
"は試験の中で作り、repo に置かない。"
msgstr ""
"**Adding tests**: Add a `*.spec.ts` under `e2e/tests/`. Put pages with "
"`place` from `helpers.ts`, and select the regions (toolbar, filters, list, "
"viewer, and the Key view's file box and upload box) with the functions in "
"`helpers.ts`. Put files with `placeFile`; a test of the upload box hands a "
"file to `input[type=file]` with `setInputFiles`. The tests run one at a time "
"against the same store, so use a different project name in each test. A test "
"that looks at new arrivals (the list column being replaced and the new-"
"arrival mark) opens the UI with `openLive` before putting a page (the notice "
"for a page put before the connection is made never arrives). The new-arrival "
"mark appears while the list column is scrolled down, so scroll it with "
"`scrollList` before putting a page. Create large files inside the test; do "
"not put them in the repo."

#: src/development.md
msgid ""
"**返事の状態を見る試験**（`e2e/tests/reply.spec.ts`）: 返事待ちの数は、絞り込"
"みに関わらず置き場の全部を数え、tab の題にも出る。試験は同じ置き場に順に流れ"
"るので、返事待ちにしたページは、試験の終わりまでに答えたにする（残すと、後の"
"試験の tab の題が変わる）。絞り込みの列の見出し「返事」は、状態を書いたページ"
"が 1 枚でもあると出るので、この file は、見出しの並びを見る `list.spec.ts` よ"
"り後に流れる名にしてある。"
msgstr ""
"**Tests of the reply state** (`e2e/tests/reply.spec.ts`): the waiting count "
"covers the whole store regardless of filters and also shows in the tab "
"title. The tests run in order against the same store, so a page marked as "
"waiting must be marked as answered by the end of its test (leaving it "
"changes the tab title for later tests). The filter-column heading for the "
"reply state appears as soon as one page has that state written, so this file "
"is named to run after `list.spec.ts`, which checks the order of the headings."

#: src/development.md
msgid ""
"**送り手を見る試験**（`e2e/tests/list.spec.ts` の終わり）: 試験の置き場は、次"
"の port の偽の castlist に送り手を聞き、一覧の UI の link の頭"
"（`PAGETRAY_CASTLIST_LINK_URL`）は、聞く先と別の値（`helpers.ts` の "
"`CASTLIST_LINK`。開かない）にする（`playwright.config.ts`）。偽の castlist "
"は `helpers.ts` の `startCastlist` で、送り手を書いて置く間だけ立てる。送り手"
"のある行が 1 つでもあると、絞り込みの列に見出し「送り手」が出るので、見出しの"
"並びを見る試験より後に置く。"
msgstr ""
"**Tests of senders** (at the end of `e2e/tests/list.spec.ts`): the test "
"store asks a fake castlist on the next port for senders, and the base of the "
"links in the list UI (`PAGETRAY_CASTLIST_LINK_URL`) is set to a value "
"different from that address (`CASTLIST_LINK` in `helpers.ts`; never opened) "
"(`playwright.config.ts`). The fake castlist is `startCastlist` in "
"`helpers.ts`, and it runs only while pages with a sender are being put. The "
"filter-column heading for senders appears as soon as one row has a sender, "
"so these tests come after the test that checks the order of the headings."

#: src/development.md
msgid ""
"**template を変えた時**: `templates/index.html` を変えたら、この試験も流す。"
"試験が選ぶ手がかり（区画の id の `toolbar`・`filters`・`list`・`viewer`・"
"`files`・`upload`、`#fresh`・`#waiting`、`li[data-path]`・`.reply`、絞り込み"
"の列の見出しの字など）を変える時は、同じ PR で `helpers.ts` も直す。"
msgstr ""
"**When you change the template**: After changing `templates/index.html`, run "
"these tests too. When you change something the tests select by (the region "
"ids `toolbar`, `filters`, `list`, `viewer`, `files`, and `upload`, `#fresh` "
"and `#waiting`, `li[data-path]` and `.reply`, the heading text of the "
"filters, and so on), fix `helpers.ts` in the same PR."

#: src/development.md
msgid ""
"**Node の依存**: 依存は `@playwright/test` の 1 つで、版は `package.json` に"
"そのまま書く（`^` を付けない）。`pnpm-lock.yaml` を commit し、CI は `--"
"frozen-lockfile` で入れる。`pnpm-workspace.yaml` の `minimumReleaseAge` が、"
"公開から 2 日たっていない版を入れさせない。弱点は、workflow の `advisories` "
"が `pnpm audit` で、PR ごとと週に 1 度見る。版は手で上げる（Playwright を上げ"
"ると browser も替わるので、試験が通るのを見る）。`package.json` の版を書き替"
"え、`pnpm install` → 試験 → PR。"
msgstr ""
"**Node dependencies**: There is one dependency, `@playwright/test`, and its "
"version is written exactly in `package.json` (no `^`). `pnpm-lock.yaml` is "
"committed, and CI installs with `--frozen-lockfile`. `minimumReleaseAge` in "
"`pnpm-workspace.yaml` keeps out versions published less than 2 days ago. For "
"vulnerabilities, the workflow's `advisories` job runs `pnpm audit` on every "
"PR and once a week. Versions are raised by hand (raising Playwright also "
"changes the browser, so watch the tests pass): rewrite the version in "
"`package.json`, then `pnpm install` → tests → PR."

#: src/development.md
msgid "この本を直す"
msgstr "Editing this book"

#: src/development.md
msgid ""
"この本は [mdBook](https://rust-lang.github.io/mdBook/) で作り、release の tag"
"（`v*`）を打った時に、workflow（`.github/workflows/docs.yml`）が GitHub "
"Pages に出す。PR と main への push では、build できるか・英語の訳が原文と合っ"
"ているか・作った本が browser で動くか（下の「本の試験」）を見る（job の名は "
"`docs`）。"
msgstr ""
"This book is built with [mdBook](https://rust-lang.github.io/mdBook/), and "
"the workflow (`.github/workflows/docs.yml`) publishes it to GitHub Pages "
"when a release tag (`v*`) is pushed. On PRs and pushes to main, it checks "
"that the book builds, that the English translation matches the source text, "
"and that the built book works in a browser (\"Book tests\" below); the job "
"is named `docs`."

#: src/development.md
msgid "`docs/book.toml`"
msgstr "`docs/book.toml`"

#: src/development.md
msgid "本の設定。組み込みの検索は切ってある（日本語が引けないため）"
msgstr ""
"The book's configuration. The built-in search is turned off (because it "
"cannot search Japanese)"

#: src/development.md
msgid "`docs/src/`"
msgstr "`docs/src/`"

#: src/development.md
msgid ""
"原文（日本語）。目次は `SUMMARY.md`。語の決まりは `glossary.md`（用語集）"
msgstr ""
"The source text (Japanese). The table of contents is `SUMMARY.md`. The rules "
"for terms are in `glossary.md` (the Glossary)"

#: src/development.md
msgid "`docs/po/en.po`"
msgstr "`docs/po/en.po`"

#: src/development.md
msgid "英語の訳。原文の段落・表の升・コードの塊ごとに 1 項"
msgstr ""
"The English translation. One entry per paragraph, table cell, or code block "
"of the source text"

#: src/development.md
msgid "`docs/theme/site.js`・`site.css`"
msgstr "`docs/theme/site.js`, `site.css`"

#: src/development.md
msgid "上の帯に足す、言葉の切り替えと検索の枠"
msgstr "The language switcher and the search box added to the menu bar"

#: src/development.md
msgid "`docs/pagefind.yml`"
msgstr "`docs/pagefind.yml`"

#: src/development.md
msgid "検索（[Pagefind](https://pagefind.app/)）の索引に入れる物"
msgstr "What goes into the search ([Pagefind](https://pagefind.app/)) index"

#: src/development.md
msgid "`docs/mermaid.min.js`・`mermaid-init.js`"
msgstr "`docs/mermaid.min.js`, `mermaid-init.js`"

#: src/development.md
msgid "図（Mermaid）を描く script。`mdbook-mermaid install docs` が置いた物"
msgstr ""
"Scripts that render diagrams (Mermaid). Placed by `mdbook-mermaid install "
"docs`"

#: src/development.md
msgid "`ci/docs-po.sh`"
msgstr "`ci/docs-po.sh`"

#: src/development.md
msgid "`en.po` を原文に合わせる。`--check` を付けると、合っているかを見るだけ"
msgstr ""
"Syncs `en.po` with the source text. With `--check`, it only verifies that "
"they match"

#: src/development.md
msgid "`ci/docs-build.sh`"
msgstr "`ci/docs-build.sh`"

#: src/development.md
msgid ""
"日本語の本を `docs/book/` に、英語の本を `docs/book/en/` に作り、検索の索引"
"を `docs/book/pagefind/` に作る"
msgstr ""
"Builds the Japanese book into `docs/book/`, the English book into `docs/book/"
"en/`, and the search index into `docs/book/pagefind/`"

#: src/development.md
msgid ""
"道具は、workflow の `env` に書いた版を入れる（上げる時は、workflow の版と "
"checksum を一緒に上げる）。"
msgstr ""
"Install the tools at the versions written in the workflow's `env` (when "
"updating, bump the version and the checksum in the workflow together)."

#: src/development.md
msgid ""
"`ci/docs-build.sh` が本を `docs/book/` に作る。最後の行で配り、`http://"
"localhost:8000/` で見る。"
msgstr ""
"`ci/docs-build.sh` builds the book into `docs/book/`. The last line serves "
"it; open `http://localhost:8000/` to view it."

#: src/development.md
msgid ""
"**mdbook-i18n-helpers は commit を名指して入れる**: 公開済みの 0.4.0 は、訳し"
"た本で囲み（`> [!WARNING]` など）を崩す。直し（[\\#344](https://github.com/"
"google/mdbook-i18n-helpers/pull/344)）を含む版が出たら、版の名指しに替える。"
msgstr ""
"**mdbook-i18n-helpers is installed by pinning a commit**: The published "
"0.4.0 breaks admonitions (`> [!WARNING]` and the like) in the translated "
"book. Once a version containing the fix ([\\#344](https://github.com/google/"
"mdbook-i18n-helpers/pull/344)) is released, switch to pinning a version."

#: src/development.md
msgid ""
"**原文を直したら、同じ PR で英語も直す**: `ci/docs-po.sh` を流すと、足した段"
"落が `docs/po/en.po` に空の訳で入り、変えた段落に `#, fuzzy` の印が付く。空の"
"所と印の所を訳し、印の行を消す。`ci/docs-po.sh --check` が通れば済み（CI も同"
"じ検査を流す。原文にあって訳に無い段落・`fuzzy` の残り・訳に残った日本語があ"
"ると落ちる）。"
msgstr ""
"**When you edit the source text, update the English in the same PR**: "
"running `ci/docs-po.sh` adds new paragraphs to `docs/po/en.po` with an empty "
"translation and marks changed paragraphs with `#, fuzzy`. Translate the "
"empty and marked entries, and delete the marker lines. You are done when `ci/"
"docs-po.sh --check` passes (CI runs the same check; it fails on a source "
"paragraph with no translation, a leftover `fuzzy` marker, or Japanese left "
"in a translation)."

#: src/development.md
msgid ""
"**コードの塊**: 訳に出るのは、コードの中の註（`#` の行）と、引用符の中の字だ"
"け。命令の中の置き換えの名は訳せないので、`<version>` のように英字で書く。行"
"の後ろに付けた註は、取り出されないことがある（`ci/docs-build.sh` が、英語の本"
"に日本語が残っていれば落ちる）。"
msgstr ""
"**Code blocks**: only comments (lines starting with `#`) and text inside "
"quotes are extracted for translation. Placeholders inside commands cannot be "
"translated, so write them in ASCII, such as `<version>`. A comment at the "
"end of a command line is sometimes not extracted (`ci/docs-build.sh` fails "
"if Japanese is left in the English book)."

#: src/development.md
msgid ""
"**訳さない物も `msgstr` に書く**: 命令・URL だけの項は、原文をそのまま写す。"
"link の先の file の名（`run.md` など）は変えない。見出しを指す `#…` は、英語"
"の本では見出しの id が訳した題から作られるので、訳した見出しの id に書き替え"
"る（`release.md#image-に入る物` → `release.md#what-goes-into-the-image`）。"
msgstr ""
"**Fill in `msgstr` even for entries you do not translate**: for command-only "
"and URL-only entries, copy the source text as is. Do not change the file "
"name of a link target (such as `run.md`). For a `#…` that points to a "
"heading, rewrite it to the id of the translated heading, because in the "
"English book heading ids are generated from the translated titles (for "
"example, the link to the \"What goes into the image\" section becomes "
"`release.md#what-goes-into-the-image`)."

#: src/development.md
msgid ""
"**語を足す・替える**: 先に [用語集](glossary.md) を直し、文書・註・code の名"
"をそれに合わせる。用語集に書いた id が画面に在るか・「使わない言い方」が戻っ"
"ていないかは、試験（`tests/terms.rs`）が見る。"
msgstr ""
"**Adding or changing a term**: First fix the [Glossary](glossary.md), then "
"make the documents, comments, and names in the code match it. A test (`tests/"
"terms.rs`) checks that the ids written in the glossary exist in the UI and "
"that the \"terms to avoid\" have not come back."

#: src/development.md
msgid ""
"**章を足す**: `docs/src/` に file を置き、`SUMMARY.md` に 1 行足す。CLI の章"
"は `docs/src/cli.md`（「使う」の節の、動かす と API の仕様 の間）。"
msgstr ""
"**Add a chapter**: Put a file in `docs/src/` and add one line to "
"`SUMMARY.md`. The CLI chapter is `docs/src/cli.md` (in the \"Usage\" "
"section, between Running and API specification)."

#: src/development.md
msgid ""
"**repo の file を指す link**: 本の外の file（`CHANGELOG.md` など）は、GitHub "
"の URL で書く。章どうしは、`run.md` のように file の名で書く。"
msgstr ""
"**Links to files in the repo**: For files outside the book (such as "
"`CHANGELOG.md`), use the GitHub URL. Between chapters, use the file name, as "
"in `run.md`."

#: src/development.md
msgid ""
"**本の試験**: `e2e/docs-tests/` の試験（Playwright）が、作った本を本物の "
"browser で開き、どの章も開いて console に誤りが無いこと・図が描けること・検索"
"の枠が開いて日本語と英語の語が当たること・言葉の切り替えで同じ章へ移ることを"
"見る。`ci/docs-build.sh` の後に、`e2e/` で `pnpm test:docs` を打つ（道具の入"
"れ方は上の「一覧の UI の試験」と同じ）。CI では job `docs` が流す。章を足した"
"ら、`e2e/docs-tests/docs.spec.ts` の章の一覧にも足す（目次と合わないと落ち"
"る）。"
msgstr ""
"**Book tests**: The tests in `e2e/docs-tests/` (Playwright) open the built "
"book in a real browser and check that every chapter opens with no errors in "
"the console, that the diagrams render, that the search box opens and finds "
"Japanese and English words, and that the language switcher moves to the same "
"chapter. After `ci/docs-build.sh`, run `pnpm test:docs` in `e2e/` (the tools "
"are installed the same way as in \"List UI tests\" above). In CI, the `docs` "
"job runs them. When you add a chapter, also add it to the chapter list in "
"`e2e/docs-tests/docs.spec.ts` (the test fails if it does not match the table "
"of contents)."

#: src/development.md
msgid ""
"**図**: ```` ```mermaid ```` の塊で書く。構文を間違えても build は通る。描け"
"るかは、本の試験が見る（図のある章は `docs.spec.ts` の `FIGURES` に並べる。図"
"を足した章は、そこにも足す）。"
msgstr ""
"**Diagrams**: Write them in ```` ```mermaid ```` blocks. The build passes "
"even if the syntax is wrong. The book tests check that they render (the "
"chapters with diagrams are listed in `FIGURES` in `docs.spec.ts`; when you "
"add a diagram to a chapter, add the chapter there too)."

#: src/development.md
msgid ""
"**検索と言葉の切り替え**: `docs/theme/site.js` は、mdBook の画面の `#mdbook-"
"menu-bar` と `path_to_root` に頼っている。mdBook を上げても検索の枠が開くこ"
"と・言葉が切り替わることは、本の試験が見る。"
msgstr ""
"**Search and the language switcher**: `docs/theme/site.js` depends on "
"`#mdbook-menu-bar` and `path_to_root` in mdBook's page. The book tests check "
"that the search box still opens and that the language still switches after "
"mdBook is updated."

#: src/db.md
msgid ""
"置き場は、ページと file を SQLite の file 1 つに持つ（置き場所は [動かす]"
"(run.md) の表の「DB」）。この章は、その中の表・列・一意と索引と、表どうしの結"
"びを書く。読む人は、SQL を直す人と、[写し](run.md#db-の写しを取る) を "
"`sqlite3` で開いて調べる人。"
msgstr ""
"The store keeps pages and files in a single SQLite file (where it lives is "
"in the \"DB\" row of the table in [Running](run.md)). This chapter describes "
"its tables, columns, unique constraints and indexes, and how the tables "
"relate. It is for people who change the SQL and for people who open a "
"[backup](run.md#back-up-the-db) with `sqlite3` to look into it."

#: src/db.md
msgid ""
"**表を作るのは `migrations/` の SQL**: サーバーが起きる時に、まだ当てていない"
"物を当てる。当てた SQL は変えず、次の番号の file を足す（[開発]"
"(development.md) の「当てた移行の SQL は変えない」）。SQL の註には古い語が残"
"ることがある（`0001_init.sql` と `0003_files.sql` の `key` の註の「鍵」は、今"
"の語では Key）。"
msgstr ""
"**The SQL in `migrations/` creates the tables**: On startup, the server "
"applies those not yet applied. Applied SQL is never edited; add a file with "
"the next number instead (\"Never change an applied migration\" in "
"[Development](development.md)). The comments in the SQL may keep old wording "
"(the comment on `key` in `0001_init.sql` and `0003_files.sql` uses an old "
"word for what is now called Key)."

#: src/db.md
msgid ""
"**この章と本物の DB は、試験が突き合わせる**: `tests/schema_doc.rs` が、移行"
"を当てた DB の表・列・型・空を許すか・主キーと一意と索引を、この章と比べる。"
"表や列を変えたら、同じ PR でこの章も直す。試験が読むので、表ごとの節の形（見"
"出し・列の表・「主キー:」「一意:」「索引:」の行）は崩さない。"
msgstr ""
"**A test compares this chapter with the real DB**: `tests/schema_doc.rs` "
"compares the tables, columns, types, nullability, primary keys, unique "
"constraints, and indexes of the migrated DB with this chapter. When you "
"change a table or a column, update this chapter in the same PR. The test "
"reads the Japanese source, so keep the shape of each table's section (the "
"heading, the column table, and the primary key, unique, and index lines)."

#: src/db.md
msgid ""
"どの表も `strict`（列の型に合わない値は入らない）。時刻はみな UTC の ISO の形"
"の字（`2026-11-21T12:34:56.789Z`）。"
msgstr ""
"Every table is `strict` (a value that does not match the column type is "
"rejected). All times are UTC ISO strings (`2026-11-21T12:34:56.789Z`)."

#: src/db.md
msgid "表どうしの結び"
msgstr "How the tables relate"

#: src/db.md
msgid ""
"```mermaid\n"
"erDiagram\n"
"  pages ||--|| pages_fts : \"id = rowid\"\n"
"  pages }o..o{ removed : \"同じ project・Key・種類で番号を分ける\"\n"
"  pages }o..o{ files : \"同じ project・Key\"\n"
"  files }o..o{ files_removed : \"同じ project・Key・名・拡張子で番号を分ける"
"\"\n"
"  senders |o--o{ pages : \"pages.sender_id = id\"\n"
"  senders |o--o{ files : \"files.sender_id = id\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```mermaid\n"
"erDiagram\n"
"  pages ||--|| pages_fts : \"id = rowid\"\n"
"  pages }o..o{ removed : \"share numbers per project, Key, and kind\"\n"
"  pages }o..o{ files : \"same project and Key\"\n"
"  files }o..o{ files_removed : \"share numbers per project, Key, name, and "
"extension\"\n"
"  senders |o--o{ pages : \"pages.sender_id = id\"\n"
"  senders |o--o{ files : \"files.sender_id = id\"\n"
"```"

#: src/db.md
msgid ""
"**外部キーは 2 つだけ**（0.6.0 から）: `pages.sender_id` と "
"`files.sender_id` が `senders.id` を指す（`on delete restrict on update "
"restrict`）。ほかの表どうしは、同じ値（project・Key など）で結ぶだけで、結び"
"は `src/db.rs` の SQL が守る。"
msgstr ""
"**There are only two foreign keys** (since 0.6.0): `pages.sender_id` and "
"`files.sender_id` reference `senders.id` (`on delete restrict on update "
"restrict`). Other tables relate only by sharing values (project, Key, and so "
"on), and the SQL in `src/db.rs` keeps them consistent."

#: src/db.md
msgid ""
"**接続ごとの決まり**: `Db::open` が、読む接続にも書く接続にも `PRAGMA "
"foreign_keys = ON` と `PRAGMA recursive_triggers = ON` を付ける（SQLite で"
"は、どちらも接続ごとに効く）。移行を当てた後に `PRAGMA foreign_key_check` を"
"流し、合わない行が 1 つでもあれば、サーバーは起きない。"
msgstr ""
"**Per-connection settings**: `Db::open` sets `PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON` and "
"`PRAGMA recursive_triggers = ON` on both the reading and the writing "
"connections (in SQLite, both take effect per connection). After applying the "
"migrations it runs `PRAGMA foreign_key_check`, and if even one row fails the "
"check, the server does not start."

#: src/db.md
msgid ""
"**送り手**: ページや file を置く時に、呼ぶ側が付随する id を書けば、"
"`senders` に 1 行足し、ページや file の行から指す（同じ取引）。`senders` は足"
"すだけの表で、書き換えも消しも trigger が断る。ページや file を消しても、送り"
"手の行は残る。"
msgstr ""
"**Senders**: when a page or a file is put and the caller writes an attached "
"id, one row is added to `senders` and the page or file row points to it (in "
"the same transaction). `senders` is an append-only table; triggers reject "
"both updates and deletes. Deleting a page or a file leaves its sender row."

#: src/db.md
msgid ""
"**番号**: ページの番号は、`pages` と `removed` の両方の、同じ project・Key・"
"種類の番号の最大 ＋ 1。file も同じく、`files` と `files_removed` から取る。だ"
"から消した番号は 2 度使わない。書く接続は 1 本なので、番号を取る所は 1 列に並"
"ぶ。"
msgstr ""
"**Numbers**: A page's number is the largest number for the same project, "
"Key, and kind across both `pages` and `removed`, plus 1. Files work the same "
"way, using `files` and `files_removed`. So a removed number is never used "
"again. There is only one writing connection, so taking numbers happens one "
"at a time."

#: src/db.md
msgid ""
"**消す**: 1 つの取引で、番号を `removed`（file は `files_removed`）に写し、"
"`pages_fts` と `pages`（file は `files`）の行を消す。本文は残さない。"
msgstr ""
"**Delete**: In a single transaction, copies the number into `removed` "
"(`files_removed` for files) and deletes the rows in `pages_fts` and `pages` "
"(`files` for files). The body is not kept."

#: src/db.md
msgid ""
"**ページと file**: ページの本文は file を path（`files/<語>-<n>.<拡張子>`）で"
"参照するだけで、DB の中では結ばない。片方を消しても、もう片方は残る。"
msgstr ""
"**Pages and files**: A page body refers to a file only by its path (`files/"
"<word>-<n>.<extension>`); the DB does not link them. Deleting one leaves the "
"other."

#: src/db.md
msgid "`pages` — ページ"
msgstr "`pages` — pages"

#: src/db.md
msgid ""
"置かれたページ 1 枚が 1 行。置き直すと、別の番号の別の行になる。置いた後に書"
"き換わるのは、返事の状態の 2 つの列（`asked_at`・`answered_at`）だけ。"
msgstr ""
"One row per stored page. Putting it again makes a different row with a "
"different number. After a page is put, only the two reply-state columns "
"(`asked_at`, `answered_at`) are ever rewritten."

#: src/db.md
msgid "列"
msgstr "Column"

#: src/db.md
msgid "型"
msgstr "Type"

#: src/db.md
msgid "空"
msgstr "Null"

#: src/db.md src/glossary.md
msgid "意味"
msgstr "Meaning"

#: src/db.md
msgid "`id`"
msgstr "`id`"

#: src/db.md
msgid "integer"
msgstr "integer"

#: src/db.md
msgid "不可"
msgstr "no"

#: src/db.md
msgid "行の番号。`pages_fts` の `rowid` と同じ"
msgstr "Row number. Same as `rowid` in `pages_fts`"

#: src/db.md src/glossary.md
msgid "`project`"
msgstr "`project`"

#: src/db.md
msgid "text"
msgstr "text"

#: src/db.md
msgid "project の名（URL の 1 段目）"
msgstr "Project name (the first level of the URL)"

#: src/db.md src/glossary.md
msgid "`key`"
msgstr "`key`"

#: src/db.md
msgid "Key（URL の 2 段目）"
msgstr "Key (the second level of the URL)"

#: src/db.md src/glossary.md
msgid "`kind`"
msgstr "`kind`"

#: src/db.md
msgid "種類の名"
msgstr "Kind name"

#: src/db.md
msgid "番号（project・Key・種類ごとに 1 から）"
msgstr "Number (from 1 per project, Key, and kind)"

#: src/db.md
msgid "`title`"
msgstr "`title`"

#: src/db.md
msgid "本文の `<title>` から取った題"
msgstr "Title taken from the body's `<title>`"

#: src/db.md src/glossary.md
msgid "`role`"
msgstr "`role`"

#: src/db.md
msgid "置いた人の役割（わからなければ `unknown`）"
msgstr "Role of whoever put it (`unknown` if not known)"

#: src/db.md
msgid "置いた人の workspace の ID（わからなければ空の字）"
msgstr "Workspace ID of whoever put it (an empty string if not known)"

#: src/db.md
msgid "置いた時刻"
msgstr "Time it was put"

#: src/db.md src/glossary.md
msgid "`body`"
msgstr "`body`"

#: src/db.md
msgid "blob"
msgstr "blob"

#: src/db.md
msgid "本文。置かれた HTML をそのまま"
msgstr "The body: the HTML exactly as put"

#: src/db.md
msgid "可"
msgstr "yes"

#: src/db.md
msgid "返事待ちにした時刻。返事を求めていなければ空（0.5.0 から）"
msgstr ""
"When the page was marked as waiting for a reply. Null if no reply was asked "
"for (since 0.5.0)"

#: src/db.md
msgid "答えた時刻。まだ答えていなければ空（0.5.0 から）"
msgstr "When it was answered. Null if not answered yet (since 0.5.0)"

#: src/db.md
msgid "`sender_id`"
msgstr "`sender_id`"

#: src/db.md
msgid ""
"送り手（`senders.id`）。付随する id を書かずに置いたページと、0.6.0 より前に"
"置かれたページは空"
msgstr ""
"Sender (`senders.id`). Null for pages put without an attached id and for "
"pages put before 0.6.0"

#: src/db.md
msgid "主キー: `(id)`"
msgstr "Primary key: `(id)`"

#: src/db.md
msgid "一意: `(project, key, kind, n)`"
msgstr "Unique: `(project, key, kind, n)`"

#: src/db.md
msgid "索引: `pages_created` `(created_at)`"
msgstr "Index: `pages_created` `(created_at)`"

#: src/db.md
msgid "索引: `pages_waiting` `(asked_at)`"
msgstr "Index: `pages_waiting` `(asked_at)`"

#: src/db.md
msgid "索引: `pages_sender` `(sender_id)`"
msgstr "Index: `pages_sender` `(sender_id)`"

#: src/db.md
msgid ""
"`pages_waiting` は、返事待ち（`asked_at` があり、`answered_at` が空）の行だけ"
"の索引。"
msgstr ""
"`pages_waiting` is an index over only the rows waiting for a reply "
"(`asked_at` set, `answered_at` null)."

#: src/db.md
msgid ""
"書く所: `Db::put`・`Db::set_reply`（返事の状態だけ）。読む所: `Db::body`・"
"`Db::list`・`Db::facets`。消す所: `Db::remove`。"
msgstr ""
"Written by `Db::put` and `Db::set_reply` (the reply state only). Read by "
"`Db::body`, `Db::list`, `Db::facets`. Deleted by `Db::remove`."

#: src/db.md
msgid ""
"**返事の状態**: `asked_at` も `answered_at` も空なら、返事を求めていないペー"
"ジ。`asked_at` があり `answered_at` が空なら返事待ち。`answered_at` があれば"
"答えた。0.5.0 より前に置かれたページは、どちらも空。"
msgstr ""
"**Reply state**: with both `asked_at` and `answered_at` null, no reply was "
"asked for. With `asked_at` set and `answered_at` null, the page is waiting "
"for a reply. With `answered_at` set, it has been answered. Pages put before "
"0.5.0 have both null."

#: src/db.md
msgid "`pages_fts` — 全文の索引"
msgstr "`pages_fts` — full-text index"

#: src/db.md
msgid ""
"[全文の索引](glossary.md)（SQLite の FTS5 の仮想の表）。`tokenize='trigram'` "
"で字を 3 字ずつに切るので、日本語の語も引ける。ページ 1 枚が 1 行で、`rowid` "
"が `pages.id`。"
msgstr ""
"The [full-text index](glossary.md) (an SQLite FTS5 virtual table). "
"`tokenize='trigram'` splits text into 3-character pieces, so Japanese words "
"can be looked up too. One row per page, and `rowid` is `pages.id`."

#: src/db.md
msgid "`pages.title` の写し"
msgstr "Copy of `pages.title`"

#: src/db.md
msgid "`text`"
msgstr "`text`"

#: src/db.md
msgid ""
"本文から tag・script・style を除いた字（`src/text.rs`）。本文そのものは持たな"
"い"
msgstr ""
"Body text with tags, scripts, and styles removed (`src/text.rs`). The body "
"itself is not kept here"

#: src/db.md
msgid ""
"書く所: `Db::put`（`pages` と同じ取引）。読む所: `Db::list`（探す語が 3 字以"
"上なら索引で引き、短い語があれば端から見る）。消す所: `Db::remove`。"
msgstr ""
"Written by `Db::put` (in the same transaction as `pages`). Read by "
"`Db::list` (uses the index when every search word has 3 or more characters, "
"and scans when a word is shorter). Deleted by `Db::remove`."

#: src/db.md
msgid ""
"FTS5 が、中身を持つ影の表（`pages_fts_data`・`pages_fts_idx`・"
"`pages_fts_content`・`pages_fts_docsize`・`pages_fts_config`）を作る。手で触"
"らない。"
msgstr ""
"FTS5 creates shadow tables that hold the contents (`pages_fts_data`, "
"`pages_fts_idx`, `pages_fts_content`, `pages_fts_docsize`, "
"`pages_fts_config`). Do not touch them by hand."

#: src/db.md
msgid "`removed` — 消したページの番号"
msgstr "`removed` — numbers of removed pages"

#: src/db.md
msgid ""
"消したページ 1 枚が 1 行。本文は持たない。同じ番号を 2 度使わない（古い URL "
"が別のページを指さない）ためと、消したページの URL に `410` を返すため。"
msgstr ""
"One row per removed page, without the body. Kept so that no number is used "
"twice (an old URL never points to a different page) and so that a removed "
"page's URL returns `410`."

#: src/db.md
msgid "消したページの project"
msgstr "Project of the removed page"

#: src/db.md
msgid "消したページの Key"
msgstr "Key of the removed page"

#: src/db.md
msgid "消したページの種類"
msgstr "Kind of the removed page"

#: src/db.md
msgid "消したページの番号"
msgstr "Number of the removed page"

#: src/db.md
msgid "`removed_at`"
msgstr "`removed_at`"

#: src/db.md
msgid "消した時刻"
msgstr "Time it was removed"

#: src/db.md
msgid "主キー: `(project, key, kind, n)`"
msgstr "Primary key: `(project, key, kind, n)`"

#: src/db.md
msgid ""
"書く所: `Db::remove`。読む所: `Db::put`（番号を決める時・取り込みで名指された"
"番号を断る時）・`Db::removed_at`（`410` を返す時）。"
msgstr ""
"Written by `Db::remove`. Read by `Db::put` (when choosing a number, and when "
"refusing a number named in an import) and `Db::removed_at` (when returning "
"`410`)."

#: src/db.md
msgid "`files` — file"
msgstr "`files` — files"

#: src/db.md
msgid ""
"ページから参照する file（画像・PDF・字の file）1 つが 1 行。置き直すと、別の"
"番号の別の行になる。"
msgstr ""
"One row per file (an image, a PDF, or a text file) referenced from pages. "
"Putting it again makes a different row with a different number."

#: src/db.md
msgid "行の番号"
msgstr "Row number"

#: src/db.md
msgid "`name`"
msgstr "`name`"

#: src/db.md
msgid "名の語（拡張子と番号を除いた所）"
msgstr "Name word (the part without the extension and number)"

#: src/db.md
msgid "`ext`"
msgstr "`ext`"

#: src/db.md
msgid "拡張子（受ける物の一覧は `crates/api` が持つ）"
msgstr "Extension (the accepted list is in `crates/api`)"

#: src/db.md
msgid "番号（project・Key・名・拡張子ごとに 1 から）"
msgstr "Number (from 1 per project, Key, name, and extension)"

#: src/db.md
msgid "`type`"
msgstr "`type`"

#: src/db.md
msgid "返す時の `Content-Type`（拡張子から決まる）"
msgstr "`Content-Type` used when serving it (decided by the extension)"

#: src/db.md
msgid "`size`"
msgstr "`size`"

#: src/db.md
msgid "byte の数"
msgstr "Number of bytes"

#: src/db.md
msgid "`sha256`"
msgstr "`sha256`"

#: src/db.md
msgid "中身の SHA-256（16 進の小文字）"
msgstr "SHA-256 of the contents (lowercase hex)"

#: src/db.md
msgid "中身をそのまま"
msgstr "The contents exactly as put"

#: src/db.md
msgid ""
"送り手（`senders.id`）。付随する id を書かずに置いた file・一覧の UI から上げ"
"た file・0.6.0 より前に置かれた file は空"
msgstr ""
"Sender (`senders.id`). Null for files put without an attached id, files "
"uploaded from the list UI, and files put before 0.6.0"

#: src/db.md
msgid "一意: `(project, key, name, ext, n)`"
msgstr "Unique: `(project, key, name, ext, n)`"

#: src/db.md
msgid "索引: `files_created` `(created_at)`"
msgstr "Index: `files_created` `(created_at)`"

#: src/db.md
msgid "索引: `files_sender` `(sender_id)`"
msgstr "Index: `files_sender` `(sender_id)`"

#: src/db.md
msgid ""
"書く所: `Db::put_file`。読む所: `Db::file_body`・`Db::list_files`。消す所: "
"`Db::remove_files`。"
msgstr ""
"Written by `Db::put_file`. Read by `Db::file_body`, `Db::list_files`. "
"Deleted by `Db::remove_files`."

#: src/db.md
msgid "`files_removed` — 消した file の番号"
msgstr "`files_removed` — numbers of removed files"

#: src/db.md
msgid "消した file 1 つが 1 行。中身は持たない。`removed` と同じ訳で残す。"
msgstr ""
"One row per removed file, without the contents. Kept for the same reasons as "
"`removed`."

#: src/db.md
msgid "消した file の project"
msgstr "Project of the removed file"

#: src/db.md
msgid "消した file の Key"
msgstr "Key of the removed file"

#: src/db.md
msgid "消した file の名の語"
msgstr "Name word of the removed file"

#: src/db.md
msgid "消した file の拡張子"
msgstr "Extension of the removed file"

#: src/db.md
msgid "消した file の番号"
msgstr "Number of the removed file"

#: src/db.md
msgid "主キー: `(project, key, name, ext, n)`"
msgstr "Primary key: `(project, key, name, ext, n)`"

#: src/db.md
msgid ""
"書く所: `Db::remove_files`。読む所: `Db::put_file`・`Db::file_removed_at`。"
msgstr ""
"Written by `Db::remove_files`. Read by `Db::put_file` and "
"`Db::file_removed_at`."

#: src/db.md
msgid "`senders` — 送り手"
msgstr "`senders` — senders"

#: src/db.md
msgid ""
"ページか file を置いた時の送り手 1 つが 1 行（0.6.0 から）。置く時に、呼ぶ側"
"が付随する id（`actor_issuer`・`actor_ref`）を書けば、置くたびに 1 行足す。置"
"き場に castlist の URL（[動かす](run.md) の表の「設定」）があれば、その時に "
"castlist に聞いた答え（アクターの id・名・種類）も残す。"
msgstr ""
"One row per sender of a put page or file (since 0.6.0). When the caller "
"writes an attached id (`actor_issuer`, `actor_ref`) at put time, one row is "
"added for each put. If the store has a castlist URL (\"Settings\" in the "
"table in [Running](run.md)), the answer castlist gave at that time (the "
"actor's id, name, and kind) is recorded too."

#: src/db.md
msgid "行の番号。`pages.sender_id`・`files.sender_id` が指す"
msgstr "Row number. Referenced by `pages.sender_id` and `files.sender_id`"

#: src/db.md
msgid "付随する id を出した物（`tpm` など）"
msgstr "What issued the attached id (such as `tpm`)"

#: src/db.md
msgid "付随する id（`<種類>:<値>`。`claude.session:…` など）"
msgstr "The attached id (`<type>:<value>`, such as `claude.session:…`)"

#: src/db.md
msgid "`actor_id`"
msgstr "`actor_id`"

#: src/db.md
msgid ""
"castlist のアクターの id。castlist に聞かなかった（置き場に castlist の URL "
"が無かった）時は空"
msgstr ""
"The castlist actor's id. Null when castlist was not asked (the store had no "
"castlist URL)"

#: src/db.md
msgid "`actor_name`"
msgstr "`actor_name`"

#: src/db.md
msgid "castlist のアクターの名（その時の物）。聞かなかった時は空"
msgstr ""
"The castlist actor's name (as of that time). Null when castlist was not asked"

#: src/db.md
msgid "`actor_kind`"
msgstr "`actor_kind`"

#: src/db.md
msgid "castlist のアクターの種類（`ai`・`human`）。聞かなかった時は空"
msgstr ""
"The castlist actor's kind (`ai`, `human`). Null when castlist was not asked"

#: src/db.md
msgid "castlist が答えた時刻（答えの `as_of`）。聞かなかった時は空"
msgstr ""
"When castlist answered (`as_of` in the answer). Null when castlist was not "
"asked"

#: src/db.md
msgid "行を足した時刻"
msgstr "Time the row was added"

#: src/db.md
msgid "索引: `senders_actor` `(actor_id)`"
msgstr "Index: `senders_actor` `(actor_id)`"

#: src/db.md
msgid ""
"書く所: `Db::put`・`Db::put_file`（ページや file と同じ取引）。読む所: "
"`Db::list`・`Db::list_files`・`Db::set_reply`（記録に添える）・`Db::facets`"
"（絞り込みの候補）。"
msgstr ""
"Written by `Db::put` and `Db::put_file` (in the same transaction as the page "
"or file). Read by `Db::list`, `Db::list_files`, `Db::set_reply` (added to "
"the record), `Db::facets` (filter choices)."

#: src/db.md
msgid ""
"**足すだけ**: trigger `senders_no_update`・`senders_no_delete` が、書き換えと"
"消しを `append-only: senders` で断る。前からある表（`pages`・`files` など）に"
"は trigger を付けていない（返事の状態の書き換え・消すは前のまま）。"
msgstr ""
"**Append-only**: the triggers `senders_no_update` and `senders_no_delete` "
"reject updates and deletes with `append-only: senders`. The existing tables "
"(`pages`, `files`, and so on) have no triggers (rewriting the reply state "
"and deleting work as before)."

#: src/db.md
msgid ""
"**聞けた・聞かなかった**: `actor_id`・`actor_name`・`actor_kind`・"
"`resolved_at` が空の行は、castlist に聞かなかった送り手（画面では「未確"
"認」）。castlist に聞けなかった時・castlist が知らない送り手の時は、ページも "
"file も送り手の行も、何も残さない（[API の仕様](api.md) の `POST /api/"
"pages`）。"
msgstr ""
"**Asked or not asked**: a row whose `actor_id`, `actor_name`, `actor_kind`, "
"and `resolved_at` are null is a sender for which castlist was not asked "
"(\"unconfirmed\" in the UI). When castlist could not be asked, or castlist "
"does not know the sender, nothing is kept: no page, no file, and no sender "
"row (`POST /api/pages` in the [API specification](api.md))."

#: src/db.md
msgid "`actor_id` に外部キーは無い（アクターは castlist の DB にある）。"
msgstr "`actor_id` has no foreign key (actors live in castlist's DB)."

#: src/db.md
msgid "ほかの表"
msgstr "Other tables"

#: src/db.md
msgid ""
"`_sqlx_migrations`: sqlx が持つ表。当てた移行の番号と、その SQL の SHA-384 を"
"覚えていて、起きる時に `migrations/` の file と突き合わせる。手で触らない。"
msgstr ""
"`_sqlx_migrations`: A table owned by sqlx. It records the numbers of applied "
"migrations and the SHA-384 of their SQL, and checks them against the files "
"in `migrations/` on startup. Do not touch it by hand."

#: src/db.md
msgid "`pages_fts_` で始まる表: 上の `pages_fts` の影の表。"
msgstr ""
"Tables starting with `pages_fts_`: the shadow tables of `pages_fts` above."

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"pagetray の文書・画面・code で使う語を、1 か所に並べる。語を足す・替える時"
"は、先にここを直し、文書と code をそれに合わせる。"
msgstr ""
"The terms used in pagetray's documents, UI, and code are listed here in one "
"place. When adding or changing a term, fix this page first, then make the "
"documents and the code match it."

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "**語**: 文書で使う語。かっこの中は、英語の本と code で使う語。"
msgstr "**Term**: The term used in the documents and in the code."

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"**code の名**: HTML の id（`#…`）・class（`.…`）・型・欄・命令など。無ければ"
"「—」。"
msgstr ""
"**Name in code**: An HTML id (`#…`), a class (`.…`), a type, a field, a "
"command, and so on. \"—\" if there is none."

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"**使わない言い方**: 前に使っていた語や、ほかの物と紛れる語。文書にも註にも書"
"かない。"
msgstr ""
"**Terms to avoid**: Terms used earlier, or terms that can be confused with "
"something else. They are not written in documents or comments."

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"[roster](https://github.com/uraitakahito/roster) の `tpm` の語（担当・依頼"
"書・控えなど）は、roster の docs にある。"
msgstr ""
"The terms of `tpm` in [roster](https://github.com/uraitakahito/roster) "
"(roles, briefs, local copies, and so on) are in the roster docs."

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "置き場の物"
msgstr "Things in the store"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "語"
msgstr "Term"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "code の名"
msgstr "Name in code"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "使わない言い方"
msgstr "Terms to avoid"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "置き場（store）"
msgstr "store"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "ページを DB に持ち、番号を付けて返す、このサーバーのこと"
msgstr "This server, which keeps pages in a DB, numbers them, and returns them"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "pagestore"
msgstr "pagestore"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "サーバー（server）"
msgstr "server"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "`pagetray-server`"
msgstr "`pagetray-server`"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "置き場の本体。container の中で動く binary"
msgstr "The store itself. The binary that runs inside the container"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "`pagetray`"
msgstr "`pagetray`"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "置き場を端末から操作する命令"
msgstr "The command for operating the store from a terminal"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "ページ（page）"
msgstr "page"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "`pages`"
msgstr "`pages`"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "置き場に置く HTML 1 枚。置き直すと、別の番号の別のページになる"
msgstr ""
"One HTML document put into the store. Putting it again makes a different "
"page with a different number"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "Artifact"
msgstr "Artifact"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "本文（body）"
msgstr "body"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "ページの HTML そのもの"
msgstr "The HTML of the page itself"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "ページの記録（page record）"
msgstr "page record"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "`PageRecord`"
msgstr "`PageRecord`"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"ページ 1 枚の、本文を除いた欄（project・Key・種類・番号・題・役割・"
"workspace・時刻・大きさ・path。返事の状態を書いたページには、その時刻も。送り"
"手を記録したページには、送り手も）"
msgstr ""
"The fields of one page other than its body (project, Key, kind, number, "
"title, role, workspace, time, size, path; plus the reply-state times on "
"pages where that state has been written, and the sender on pages where a "
"sender was recorded)"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "メタデータ"
msgstr "metadata"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "返事の状態（reply state）"
msgstr "Reply state"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "`asked_at`・`answered_at`"
msgstr "`asked_at`, `answered_at`"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"Product Manager の返事が要るページに、呼ぶ側が書く状態。返事待ち（`waiting`。"
"求めて、まだ答えていない）か、答えた（`answered`）。書いていないページは、返"
"事を求めていない"
msgstr ""
"The state a caller writes on a page that needs a reply from the Product "
"Manager: waiting (`waiting`: asked, not answered yet) or answered "
"(`answered`). A page where it has not been written asks for no reply"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "project"
msgstr "project"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"ページをまとめる、いちばん上の名。`tpm` は、project の folder の path から作"
"る"
msgstr ""
"The topmost name that groups pages. `tpm` builds it from the path of the "
"project folder"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "Key"
msgstr "Key"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "課題の名（`AI-22` など）。project の下でページをまとめる"
msgstr ""
"The name of an issue (such as `AI-22`). It groups pages under a project"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "鍵"
msgstr "—"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "種類（kind）"
msgstr "kind"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "ページの種類の名（`plan`・`result` など）。名の一覧は、呼ぶ側が決める"
msgstr ""
"The name of the kind of a page (such as `plan` or `result`). The caller "
"decides the list of names"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "type"
msgstr "type"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "番号（number）"
msgstr "number"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"project・Key・種類ごとに、置き場が 1 から付ける数。消した番号は 2 度使わない"
msgstr ""
"The number the store assigns, starting at 1, per project, Key, and kind. A "
"deleted number is never used twice"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "version"
msgstr "version"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "役割（role）"
msgstr "role"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"ページを置いた人の役割の名（`tpm`・`human` など）。画面の見出しは「担当者（役"
"割）」"
msgstr ""
"The name of the role of whoever put the page (such as `tpm` or `human`). The "
"heading in the UI reads \"Assignee (role)\""

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "workspace"
msgstr "workspace"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "ページを置いた人の居場所の ID"
msgstr "The ID of the workspace of whoever put the page"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "castlist"
msgstr "castlist"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "`PAGETRAY_CASTLIST_URL`・`PAGETRAY_CASTLIST_LINK_URL`"
msgstr "`PAGETRAY_CASTLIST_URL`, `PAGETRAY_CASTLIST_LINK_URL`"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"pagetray を動かす機械で、別の container として動くサーバー。アクター（Claude "
"Code の session 1 つ・Product Manager）ごとに、本当の id と名を持つ。置き場"
"は、置かれる時に、送り手が誰かを castlist に聞く（聞く先は "
"`PAGETRAY_CASTLIST_URL`）。一覧の UI は、送り手の名から castlist のアクターの"
"画面へ link する（link の頭は `PAGETRAY_CASTLIST_LINK_URL`）"
msgstr ""
"A server that runs as another container on the machine that runs pagetray. "
"It holds the true id and name of each actor (one Claude Code session, or the "
"Product Manager). When something is put, the store asks castlist who the "
"sender is (at `PAGETRAY_CASTLIST_URL`). The list UI links the sender's name "
"to the actor's page in castlist (the link base is "
"`PAGETRAY_CASTLIST_LINK_URL`)"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "アクター（actor）"
msgstr "actor"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"castlist が本当の id と名を付けた、置く人 1 人（Claude Code の session 1 つ"
"か、Product Manager）"
msgstr ""
"One person who puts things, given a true id and name by castlist (one Claude "
"Code session, or the Product Manager)"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "付随する id（attached id）"
msgstr "attached id"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "`actor_issuer`・`actor_ref`"
msgstr "`actor_issuer`, `actor_ref`"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"ほかの道具が持つ、アクターを指す id（`<種類>:<値>`。`claude.session:…` など）"
"と、それを出した物（`tpm` など）。本当の id への引き当ては castlist がする"
msgstr ""
"An id held by another tool that points to an actor (`<type>:<value>`, such "
"as `claude.session:…`), and what issued it (such as `tpm`). castlist maps it "
"to the true id"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "送り手（sender）"
msgstr "sender"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "`senders`"
msgstr "`senders`"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"ページか file を置いた時の、付随する id と、その時に castlist が答えたアク"
"ター（id・名・種類）。castlist に聞かなかった送り手は「未確認」。足すだけで、"
"書き換えも消しもしない"
msgstr ""
"The attached id given when a page or a file was put, and the actor castlist "
"answered with at that time (id, name, kind). A sender for which castlist was "
"not asked is \"unconfirmed\". Only added, never rewritten or deleted"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "file"
msgstr "file"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "`files`"
msgstr "`files`"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"ページから参照する file（画像・PDF・字の file）1 つ。置き直すと、別の番号の別"
"の file になる"
msgstr ""
"One file (an image, a PDF, or a text file) referenced from pages. Putting it "
"again makes a different file with a different number"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "消した番号（removed number）"
msgstr "removed number"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "`removed`・`files_removed`"
msgstr "`removed`, `files_removed`"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"消したページと file の番号。本文は持たない。同じ番号を 2 度使わないためと、消"
"した URL に `410` を返すために残す"
msgstr ""
"The numbers of removed pages and files, without their bodies. Kept so that "
"no number is used twice and so that a removed URL returns `410`"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "全文の索引（full-text index）"
msgstr "full-text index"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "`pages_fts`"
msgstr "`pages_fts`"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"ページの題と本文の字を、3 字ずつに切って引けるようにした索引（SQLite の "
"FTS5）。探す欄の語は、ここで引く"
msgstr ""
"An index (SQLite FTS5) that splits page titles and body text into 3-"
"character pieces for lookup. Words in the search field are looked up here"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "移行（migration）"
msgstr "migration"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"DB の表を作る・変える SQL。サーバーが起きる時に、まだ当てていない物を番号の順"
"に当てる。当てた物は変えない"
msgstr ""
"SQL that creates or changes the DB tables. On startup, the server applies "
"those not yet applied, in number order. Applied ones are never edited"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "写し（backup）"
msgstr "backup"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "`pagetray backup`"
msgstr "`pagetray backup`"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "DB をそのまま写した、SQLite の file 1 つ"
msgstr "A single SQLite file that is a copy of the DB as it is"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "バックアップ"
msgstr "—"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "API"
msgstr "API"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "`/api/…`"
msgstr "`/api/…`"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "置き場が、呼ぶ側に向けて開けている HTTP の受け先の全体"
msgstr "The whole of the HTTP receivers the store opens to callers"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "口"
msgstr "—"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "エンドポイント（endpoint）"
msgstr "endpoint"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "API の受け先の 1 つ 1 つ（`POST /api/pages` など）"
msgstr "Each single receiver of the API (such as `POST /api/pages`)"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "API の仕様（API specification）"
msgstr "API specification"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "`docs/src/api.md`"
msgstr "`docs/src/api.md`"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "呼ぶ側が頼ってよい形を書いた章"
msgstr "The chapter that describes the shapes callers may rely on"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "口の約束"
msgstr "API contract"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "API の版（API version）"
msgstr "API version"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "`API_VERSION`"
msgstr "`API_VERSION`"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"API の形を、前からある呼ぶ側が困るように変えた時だけ上げる数。どの答えにも "
"header `Pagetray-Api` で付く"
msgstr ""
"A number bumped only when the shape of the API changes in a way that breaks "
"existing callers. It is attached to every response in the `Pagetray-Api` "
"header"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "口の版"
msgstr "—"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "呼ぶ側（caller）"
msgstr "caller"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "API を呼ぶ物（CLI・roster の `tpm page` など）"
msgstr "Whatever calls the API (the CLI, `tpm page` in roster, and so on)"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "クライアント"
msgstr "client"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"区画の名は、**働き ＋ 形**（帯・列・枠）で付ける。位置（上・左・右）では呼ば"
"ない（狭い画面では、区画が縦に積まれるため）。区画を足す時も、同じ形で名を付"
"け、ここに 1 行足す。"
msgstr ""
"The regions are named by **function + shape** (bar, column, frame). They are "
"not named by position (top, left, right), because on a narrow screen the "
"regions stack vertically. When adding a region, name it in the same form and "
"add a row here."

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "一覧の UI（list UI）"
msgstr "list UI"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "`templates/index.html`"
msgstr "`templates/index.html`"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "browser で開く、置き場の画面の全体"
msgstr "The whole screen of the store, opened in a browser"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "操作の帯（toolbar）"
msgstr "toolbar"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "`#toolbar`"
msgstr "`#toolbar`"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"画面のいちばん上の横の帯。題・探す欄・並び・返事待ちの数・新着の印がある"
msgstr ""
"The horizontal bar at the very top of the screen. It holds the title, the "
"search field, the sort order, the waiting count, and the new-arrival mark"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "ヘッダー"
msgstr "header"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "絞り込みの列（filter column）"
msgstr "filter column"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "`#filters`"
msgstr "`#filters`"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"返事・送り手・役割・workspace・種類・Key・project の候補と件数が並ぶ列。候補"
"を押すと、一覧の列が絞られる"
msgstr ""
"The column listing the choices and counts for reply state, sender, role, "
"workspace, kind, Key, and project. Pressing a choice narrows the list column"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "サイドメニュー"
msgstr "side menu, sidebar"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "一覧の列（list column）"
msgstr "list column"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "`#list`"
msgstr "`#list`"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "ページの行が並ぶ列。行を押すと、そのページが本文の枠に出る"
msgstr ""
"The column listing the rows of pages. Pressing a row shows that page in the "
"viewer"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "リスト"
msgstr "—"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "本文の枠（viewer）"
msgstr "viewer"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "`#viewer`"
msgstr "`#viewer`"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "選んだページの path と本文を、1 枚だけ出す枠"
msgstr ""
"The frame that shows the path and body of the chosen page, one page only"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "右の枠"
msgstr "right frame, preview"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "Key の画面（Key view）"
msgstr "Key view"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "`KeyView`"
msgstr "`KeyView`"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"project と Key を 1 つずつ選んだ一覧の UI（`/<project>/<key>/` など）。file "
"の枠と上げる枠が足される"
msgstr ""
"The list UI with exactly one project and one Key chosen (such as `/<project>/"
"<key>/`). It adds the file box and the upload box"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "file の枠（file box）"
msgstr "file box"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "`#files`"
msgstr "`#files`"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"Key の画面で、一覧の列の下に出る枠。その Key の file が、図の見本・名・大き"
"さ・上げた人・時刻・ページから参照する path と並ぶ"
msgstr ""
"The box below the list column in the Key view. It lists the files of that "
"Key with a thumbnail, the name, the size, who uploaded it, the time, and the "
"path a page uses to refer to it"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "上げる枠（upload box）"
msgstr "upload box"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "`#upload`"
msgstr "`#upload`"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"Key の画面で、file の枠の下に出る枠。file を選ぶか落とし、見本を見て、見た印"
"を付けてから送る"
msgstr ""
"The box below the file box in the Key view. You choose or drop a file, look "
"at the preview, and send it after ticking the reviewed check"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "見た印（reviewed check）"
msgstr "reviewed check"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "`reviewed`"
msgstr "`reviewed`"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "上げる枠の「秘密が写っていないか見た」の check。付けるまで送れない"
msgstr ""
"The \"I checked that no secrets are in it\" checkbox in the upload box. "
"Nothing can be sent until it is ticked"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "絞り込み（filter）"
msgstr "filter"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "`FilterGroup`"
msgstr "`FilterGroup`"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "一覧の列に出す行を、条件で減らすこと。条件は URL に出る"
msgstr ""
"Reducing the rows shown in the list column by conditions. The conditions "
"appear in the URL"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "フィルター"
msgstr "—"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "候補（choice）"
msgstr "choice"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "`Choice`"
msgstr "`Choice`"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "絞り込みの列に出る、押せる値の 1 つ（値と件数）"
msgstr "One pressable value shown in the filter column (a value and its count)"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "facet"
msgstr "facet"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "行（row）"
msgstr "row"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "`.rows`"
msgstr "`.rows`"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"一覧の列の中の、ページ 1 枚分（時刻・Key・種類と番号・返事の印・題・役割・"
"workspace。送り手を記録したページには、送り手の castlist の名と付随する id）"
msgstr ""
"One page's worth of the list column (time, Key, kind and number, reply mark, "
"title, role, workspace; on pages where a sender was recorded, also the "
"sender's castlist name and attached id)"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "並び（sort order）"
msgstr "sort order"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "`sort`"
msgstr "`sort`"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "一覧の列の行の順。新しい順か、古い順"
msgstr "The order of the rows in the list column: newest first or oldest first"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "ソート"
msgstr "—"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "新着の印（new-arrival mark）"
msgstr "new-arrival mark"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "`#fresh`"
msgstr "`#fresh`"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"開いている間にページが置かれると、一覧の列と絞り込みの列は押さずに新しくな"
"る。一覧の列を下へ送っている時は、操作の帯にこの印が出て、押すと一覧の列の頭"
"へ送る。「続きを出す」で古い方を見ている時は、押すと読み直す。数えるのは、今"
"の絞り込みで一覧の列に入ったページだけ"
msgstr ""
"When a page is put while the screen is open, the list column and the filter "
"column are updated without pressing anything. While the list column is "
"scrolled down, this mark appears in the toolbar, and pressing it scrolls the "
"list column to its top. While an older part is shown with \"Show more\", "
"pressing it reloads. Only pages that entered the list column under the "
"current filters are counted"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "通知"
msgstr "notification"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "返事待ちの数（waiting count）"
msgstr "Waiting count"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "`#waiting`"
msgstr "`#waiting`"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"操作の帯に出る「返事待ち N 件」。返事待ちのページが置き場に 1 枚でもあると出"
"て、押すと返事待ちだけに絞る。数は、絞り込みに関わらず置き場の全部。tab の題"
"にも同じ数が出る"
msgstr ""
"The count of waiting pages shown in the toolbar. It appears when at least "
"one page in the store is waiting for a reply, and pressing it narrows the "
"list to the waiting pages. The count covers the whole store regardless of "
"filters. The tab title shows the same count"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "返事の印（reply mark）"
msgstr "Reply mark"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "`.reply`"
msgstr "`.reply`"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"返事の状態を書いたページの行に付く印。「返事待ち」か「答えた」。状態が書かれ"
"ると、押さずに替わる"
msgstr ""
"The mark on the row of a page whose reply state has been written: waiting or "
"answered. It changes without a click when the state is written"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "未読の印（unread mark）"
msgstr "unread mark"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "`.unread`"
msgstr "`.unread`"

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"まだ本文の枠に出していない、後から置かれたページの行に付く印。browser が覚え"
"る"
msgstr ""
"The mark on the row of a page that was put later and has not yet been shown "
"in the viewer. The browser remembers it"
